SPIKE: Investigate cache tag mechanism with Redis/Valkey Entity Cache

Key details
 
Description
Investigate whether Grafbase Entity Cache can support cache tag-like functionality to enable selective invalidation of cached entities stored in Redis/Valkey. The investigation should determine whether Grafbase provides any native mechanism for grouping, identifying, or selectively invalidating Entity Cache entries, and whether a custom implementation can achieve behaviour similar to cache tags
Last Comment
 
Acceptance Criteria
1. Determine whether Grafbase provides any native cache tag or tag-like functionality. 
2. Identify how Entity Cache entries are storedsin Redis/Valkey. 
3. Confirm whether Entity Cache keys are accessible or configurable 
4. Evaluate whether custom solution that can map entities to logical tags/groups. 
5. Determine whether a custom invalidator can safely invalidate targeted cache entries 
6. Document findings, limitations, and the recommended approach. 
7. Check how cache metadata internally in grafbase using Redis/Valkey and whether it supports any data structures ( SET - Unordered unique collection & ZSET- Collection with scores/order)
 
1. Review Grafbase documentation and source code for cache tag or tag-like capabilities. 
2. Inspect Redis/Valkey Entity Cache storage structure. 
3. Determine how Entity Cache keys are generated and managed 4. Investigate supported cache invalidation mechanisms. 5. Explore options for implementing cache tag-like behaviour outside of Grafbase's native functionality 6. Recommend a feasible approach based on the findings.


